            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0657" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/8–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-01T19:00:00-04:00">August 1, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1897. Presidential Directive interpreting prior Directive of July 5, 1945 has
                    been issued to JCS. With respect to Brazil interpretation specifically
                    authorizes as lend-leasable the hospitalization of wounded, transport of
                    Brazilian Expeditionary Force to Brazil, return of military personnel being
                    trained in the US, transfers for naval and air patrols, transfers to be used
                    directly in support of redeployment (air sea rescue, ATC installations, weather
                    stations), transfers for equipping forces participating directly in the Pacific
                    Theater.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
